  "id": "hierarchical-clustering",
  "term": "hierarchical clustering",
  "definition": "Hierarchical clustering is a way of grouping data by building a layered tree of clusters, with smaller local groups organized into larger branches. In this source, it is described as combining centroid-based, model-based, and hierarchical features to form a structure of local units that can split and adapt as new data arrive.",
